{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ותרד בת פרעה", :translit "vatered bat par'oh", :gloss "and went down the daughter of Pharaoh"} {:he "ס\"ת", :translit "sa'arikh teivah", :gloss "the spelling is lengthened"} {:he "דתה", :translit "datah", :gloss "her religion"} {:he "ששינתה דתה", :translit "she'shinetah datah", :gloss "that she changed her religion"} {:he "שהלכה להתגייר", :translit "she'halchah lehitgayer", :gloss "that she went to convert"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Ba'al HaTurim reads the defective final-tav spelling of דתה as a pun: she 'changed her religion' (שינתה דתה)."}], :frame {:text "Pharaoh's daughter is later identified with the name Batyah (I Chronicles 4:18). Leviticus Rabbah 1:3 records that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to her: 'I called you Batyah — the daughter of YHWH,' honoring her for saving Moses and signifying her entry into Israel. Sotah 12b describes how the archangel Gabriel struck her attendants when they tried to stop her from taking the ark.", :sources ["Leviticus Rabbah 1:3" "Sotah 12b" "I Chronicles 4:18"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ונערותיה", :translit "ve'na'aroteha", :gloss "and her maidens"} {:he "ותקם רבקה ונערותיה", :translit "vatakam rivkah ve'na'aroteha", :gloss "and Rebecca arose and her maidens"} {:he "ונתגיירה", :translit "venitgayerah", :gloss "and she converted"} {:he "ותפשה מעשה האמהות", :translit "vatapeshah ma'aseh ha'imahot", :gloss "and she grasped the practice of the Matriarchs"} {:he "וישנה ואת נערותיה", :translit "vayeshaneh ve'et na'aroteha", :gloss "and he changed and her maidens"} {:he "וישנה", :translit "vayeshaneh", :gloss "and he changed"} {:he "ששינתה את דתה ואת נערותיה", :translit "sheshinetah et datah ve'et na'aroteha", :gloss "that she changed her religion and her maidens"} {:he "שבא המלאך והרגום", :translit "sheba hamal'ach vehargum", :gloss "that an angel came and killed them"} {:he "לפי שמנעוה לקחת התיבה", :translit "lefi sheman'u'he lekachat hateivah", :gloss "because they pr